WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.635
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is oubaitori: each in its season. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.220
Feel the surface beneath you. Unclench your jaw. Let your shoulders settle. For these five minutes, there is nowhere else you need to be.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.452
Place attention where breathing feels clearest: the nose, chest, or belly. Receive each breath without needing to hold on to it.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.446
Oubaitori names four trees: cherry, plum, peach and apricot. Each blossoms in its own season, in its own way. None of them is late. The comparison does not apply.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:00.799
A plum opening in cold air while the cherry stands bare beside it. The cherry is not failing. It is doing what it does, at the hour it does it.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:29.195
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:58.077
Notice if some part of you is running a comparison right now, even about how this is going. Let the measuring stop for a moment and just breathe.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:24.684
Now rest in a short silence. Sounds, sensations, and thoughts may come and go. Let awareness remain spacious around them.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.706
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:26.242
Notice one comparison today and set it down. Someone further along. Someone younger. Let them be in their season and stay in yours.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.752
Take one fuller breath. Feel the space beyond your body and let your eyes open in their own time. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
